{
  "category": "Mouse Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "Burrows deep underground in arid locations far from water. It only emerges to hunt for food.",
      "version": "red"
    },
    {
      "text": "Burrows deep underground in arid locations far from water. It only emerges to hunt for food.",
      "version": "blue"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its body is dry. When it gets cold at night, its hide is said to become coated with a fine dew.",
      "version": "yellow"
    },
    {
      "text": "If it fell from a great height, this POKéMON could save itself by rolling into a ball and bouncing.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "Disliking water, it lives in deep burrows in arid areas. It can roll itself instantly into a ball.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "It prefers dry, sandy places because it uses the sand to protect itself when threatened.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "SANDSHREW’s body is configured to absorb water without waste, enabling it to survive in an arid desert. This POKéMON curls up to protect itself from its enemies.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "SANDSHREW has a very dry hide that is extremely tough. The POKéMON can roll into a ball that repels any attack. At night, it burrows into the desert sand to sleep.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it curls up in a ball, it can make any attack bounce off harmlessly. Its hide has turned tough and solid as a result of living in the desert.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "It burrows and lives underground. If threatened, it curls itself up into a ball for protection.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "Burrows deep underground in arid locations far from water. It only emerges to hunt for prey.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "To protect itself from attackers, it curls up into a ball. It lives in arid regions with minimal rainfall.",
      "version": "diamond"
