    {
      "text": "Sandshrew’s body is configured to absorb water without waste, enabling it to survive in an arid desert. This Pokémon curls up to protect itself from its enemies.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sandshrew has a very dry hide that is extremely tough. The Pokémon can roll into a ball that repels any attack. At night, it burrows into the desert sand to sleep.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It can roll its body into a ball. It moves through the desert by rolling at high speeds.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It usually makes its home in deserts and arid zones, where rain does not fall. It digs holes to catch Bug-type Pokémon.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It lives in areas of limited rainfall. When danger approaches, it curls up into a ball to protect its soft stomach.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "When its skin gets wrinkled from moisture, it heads for a volcano. It lies flat on a spot with a lot of geothermal heat and dries itself out.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its body is dry. When it gets cold at night, its hide is said to become coated with a fine dew.",
      "version": "lets-go-pikachu"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its body is dry. When it gets cold at night, its hide is said to become coated with a fine dew.",
      "version": "lets-go-eevee"
    },
    {
      "text": "It loves to bathe in the grit of dry, sandy areas. By sand bathing, the Pokémon rids itself of dirt and moisture clinging to its body.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "It burrows into the ground to create its nest. If hard stones impede its tunneling, it uses its sharp claws to shatter them and then carries on digging.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
